From 2fb5412ba465adfeba1e672d34c93ef962b1ca7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] feat(core): identify the served resource in
 ScheduleRequest

ScheduleRequest only carried the tenant and the resource kind, so a
scheduler could not tell which resource an allocation belongs to and
had no way to recognise a replayed request: every reconcile pass that
reached the allocation step would allocate again (improvement plan
4.10, "allocation is not idempotent").

The request now carries a ResourceRef (kind, namespace, name, uid) and
an idempotency key. The reconciler derives the key from the resource
uid and generation (allocation_idempotency_key), so replaying a
generation - after a lost dedup key, a restart or a dropped status
write - asks for the same allocation, while a re-created resource of
the same name (new uid) asks for a new one. Resources without a uid
cannot be allocated idempotently and report Ready=False (MissingUid).

AllocationRef gains the allocated devices, and its resource_id now
names the owning resource uid. resource_kind remains readable as a
property; passing it to the constructor is rejected.
